@startuml 01_data_structures

title Core Data Structures - TrajectoryState, ErrorDynamics, ErrorState, OptimizationVariable

note as N0
  TrajectoryState, ErrorDynamics, and
  ErrorState are the "nouns" that flow
  through evaluate() and must remain JAX
  PyTrees (they are loop-carry values inside
  jit/fori_loop). Implemented natively as
  typing.NamedTuple - JAX treats NamedTuples
  as pytrees automatically, no extra packages
  (equinox/flax/chex) needed. They are
  immutable: updates go through
  state._replace(field=new_value), which is
  free at runtime (traced away by jit, same as
  the existing .at[].set() pattern).

  OptimizationVariable is build-time-only
  (never enters traced code) - NamedTuple is
  used here too for consistency, but pytree-
  ness is not required for it.
end note

class OptimizationVariable {
  +name : str
  +size : int
  +lower : array
  +upper : array
  +value : array  ' initial guess
}

note right of OptimizationVariable
  One instance per addVarGroup() call
  in the current dir_traj_opt.py.
  TOP.variables() returns a
  List<OptimizationVariable>; build_problem()
  / the pyoptsparse adapter turns this list
  into the actual optprop.addVarGroup(...)
  calls.
end note

class TrajectoryState {
  +X_hst : array          ' (N_arcs, N_subarcs+1, 7)
  +t_hst : array
  +t_node_bound : array   ' (N_arcs+1,)
}

note right of TrajectoryState
  "Where is the spacecraft" - produced by
  Propagator.propagate(). IDENTICAL shape for
  DeterministicTOP and StochasticTOP - no
  conditional/zero-filled fields needed here
  anymore, since the sensitivity terms moved
  to ErrorDynamics below.

  Known redundancy (not addressed now):
  t_node_bound/t_hst overlap somewhat - worth
  revisiting once the propagator math itself
  is reworked.
end note

class ErrorDynamics {
  +A_hst : array          ' (N_arcs, N_subarcs, 7, 7)
  +B_hst : array          ' (N_arcs, N_subarcs, 7, 3)
  +A_arc_hst : array      ' (N_arcs, 7, 7)
  +B_arc_hst : array      ' (N_arcs, 7, 3)
  +H_hst : array          ' (N_arcs, N_subarcs+1, meas_dim, 7)        -- zero for true_state
  +P_v_hst : array        ' (N_arcs, N_subarcs+1, meas_dim, meas_dim) -- zero for true_state
  +K_arc_hst : array      ' (N_arcs, 3, 7)  -- zero/unset until gain_param.compute_gains()
  +G_exe_arc_hst : array  ' (N_arcs, 3, 3)  -- zero/unset until step 4 of evaluate()
}

note right of ErrorDynamics
  The linearized perturbation model along the
  trajectory - neither "where is the
  spacecraft" (TrajectoryState) nor "what is
  the resulting error" (ErrorState), but the
  bridge between them. Stochastic-only.

  Produced by SensitivityPropagator.propagate()
  (A_hst, B_hst, A_arc_hst, B_arc_hst - zero-
  filled H_hst/P_v_hst/K_arc_hst/G_exe_arc_hst),
  then progressively filled in:
    - controller.augment_error_dynamics()
      populates H_hst/P_v_hst (EstimatedState-
      Feedback only; no-op for TrueStateFeedback)
    - gain_param.compute_gains() populates
      K_arc_hst
    - a free function (gates2Gexe_vmap) populates
      G_exe_arc_hst from inputs['U_arc_hst']
  Each step is a cheap _replace() under jit.
  By the time controller.propagate_cov() is
  called, error_dynamics is fully populated.

  G_stoch (constant process-noise covariance)
  is NOT stored here - it's a constant from
  problem_def, read directly by propagate_cov().
  Only input-dependent, per-evaluate() quantities
  live in ErrorDynamics.

  Known redundancy (not addressed now):
  A_arc_hst/B_arc_hst are in principle
  recoverable from A_hst/B_hst (full-arc
  sensitivities from sub-arc sensitivities) -
  worth revisiting once the propagator math
  itself is reworked.
end note

class ErrorState {
  +P_hst : array          ' (N_arcs, N_subarcs+1, 7, 7) -- "true" deviation covariance
  +P_U_arc_hst : array    ' (N_arcs, 3, 3)
}

note right of ErrorState
  Single concrete shape, returned identically
  by every FeedbackControlMethod - no
  subclassing needed.

  TrueStateFeedback.propagate_cov() produces
  P_hst directly (as today).

  EstimatedStateFeedback.propagate_cov()
  internally propagates the augmented 14x14
  Paug_hst (Phat/Ptild/cross-correlation
  blocks) through its EKF loop as a LOCAL
  variable that never leaves the method; at
  the end it derives, per node:
    P_hst = Phat - Phattild - Phattild.T + Ptild
  and returns ErrorState(P_hst, P_U_arc_hst) -
  the augmented representation is fully
  private to EstimatedStateFeedback.

  Renamed from "CovState" since this may later
  carry Cholesky factors or higher-order error
  terms instead of raw covariances - "Error"
  is the stable concept, "Cov" is just today's
  representation. Square-root propagation is a
  separate future effort, intentionally not
  modeled here yet.

  Because ErrorState is standardized, the
  constraints/objective terms that consume it
  (ControlNormConstraint, CovarianceConstraint,
  the J_stat objective term) are now plain
  functions of (inputs, traj_state, error_state,
  problem_def) - they do NOT need a reference
  back to the controller that produced it. See
  09_stochastic_top_composition.puml.
end note

note "K_arc_hst and G_exe_arc_hst now live as\nfields of ErrorDynamics (see above) rather than\nas transient locals - GainParameterization\n.compute_gains() and gates2Gexe_vmap()\npopulate them via _replace() before\nerror_dynamics is passed to propagate_cov()." as N1

@enduml
